{"name":"Bloodshed","hex":"#ba271a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bloodshed","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The shedding or spilling of blood.","A slaughter; destruction of life, notably on a large scale."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bloodshed"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bloodshed (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Bloodshed is an album by Brazilian death metal band Krisiun. It includes half of the Unmerciful Order EP, as well as seven new tracks. Though sometimes considered a compilation, or an EP, the band considers Bloodshed to be an album."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6f/Krisiun_-_Bloodshed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloodshed_(album)","wikidata":"Q4927999"},{"title":"Bloodshed (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Bloodshed is a Christian hardcore band established in the early 1990s. The band released a demo in 1993 and two EPs through Solid State Records. It was established in 1992 with the original lineup of Jason Fleetwood, Sean Stopnik, Jonathan Caro, Justice Gulmatico, and John Kittrell. In 1997, the band changed their name to Slingshot David, but disbanded six months later."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloodshed_(band)","wikidata":"Q25056336"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"bloodshed":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/99/En-us-bloodshed.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/99/En-us-bloodshed.ogg/En-us-bloodshed.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Rokto Snat (Blood Bath) Padak","image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3b/Rokto_Snat_%28Blood_Bath%29_Padak.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","ratio":3.8714285714285714,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.o